course: dictionary
lesson: 11614
title: Worry words in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Apprehension is a worry or fear that something bad might happen. You often feel it before something new or scary. «Mia felt apprehension before her spelling test, even though she had practised all week.» Her tummy felt funny because she was worried the test would go badly.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. Words like nervous, scared, shaking or dark tell you that apprehension is a feeling. «She walked into the dark cave with apprehension, holding her torch tight.» Try swapping in worry: «with worry» still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: In formal news, apprehension means arrest, when the police catch and take away a person. «The police made the apprehension of the man who stole the bike.» The clues are police, stole and bike, so this meaning fits. Context tells you which meaning to choose.
explain: You will often see it in phrases: feel apprehension, with apprehension, a sense of apprehension. If the sentence is about a feeling, think worry. If it is about police or a thief, check for arrest. If you are still unsure, look the word up in a dictionary.
fact: «Apprehension» means worry or fear that something bad might happen.
fact: In formal news, «apprehension» can mean the arrest of someone.
fact: «Apprehension» can also mean understanding, but this meaning is formal and rare.
fact: «With apprehension» means feeling nervous and worried.
fact: To check a meaning, swap your idea into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you are right.
exercise: «He opened the letter with apprehension, afraid of bad news.» What does apprehension mean here? | Being very tired | *Worry about something bad | Great joy and excitement | A kind of letter
exercise: «The police made the apprehension of the man who stole the bike.» In this news, what does apprehension mean? | *Arrest | A long walk | A party for the police | Winning a prize
exercise: «Ella felt a sense of apprehension as the lights went out.» Find and copy the word that names a worried feeling. | *apprehension | felt | lights | sense
test: «Before the big race, Sam felt apprehension in his tummy.» What is the closest meaning? | *Nervous worry | Excitement and joy | Sleepiness | A tall tree
test: Which phrase shows a worried feeling? | a sense of smell | a cup of tea | a sense of humour | *a sense of apprehension
exam: Ruby says apprehension is always about a prize. Is she right? | *No, it is worry or fear, and in formal news it can mean arrest | Yes, it is always a happy prize | Yes, it means a big party | No, it means a type of cloud
